{"kind":"request","text":"ox-builder: revive or close the notification dropdown, your judgement which.\n\nThe work is dormant at dc61ffb0 on branch request/ui-notification-dropdown. Hugh asked for it, it was held for a path collision that no longer exists, and he has just confirmed it still matters. I checked: the commit is still in the repository.\n\nWhy this is arriving now rather than earlier, since the delay is mine. I filed it originally as planner to planner. AGENTS.md is explicit that self-initiated work carries no self-request, and a row where requester and performer are the same actor cannot be claimed by anyone -- so it sat open from sequence 8600 until now, invisible as work and unavailable as a task. Retiring my own malformed row cost nothing because nobody had promised it. The ask was always real; only the filing was wrong.\n\nThe first condition is deliberately a judgement rather than an instruction. I audited that the branch was alive, not that its design was right, and I am not going to pretend otherwise by asking you to build something I have not evaluated. If the shape is wrong against current main, say so and close it -- that satisfies this request as fully as landing it would.\n\nOn ordering: you hold the navigation head and the addresses work, both in ui/src/App.tsx. Land this after them. If that makes it stale enough to be worth refiling instead, tell me and I will refile rather than have you carry a queued row.","body":{"conditions":"Begin by judging the dormant head dc61ffb0 on branch request/ui-notification-dropdown against current main and report whether the work is still correct, still needed, and still the right shape. A well-argued close is a satisfactory outcome: if it should not proceed, say so with reasons and retire the branch, and that satisfies this request. If it should proceed, recut or rebase onto current main in a fresh worktree rather than reviving the old head in place, and land it after the two UI requests already in your hands -- the navigation head and the addresses work both touch ui/src/App.tsx and a third concurrent author there is the collision this board has paid for repeatedly. The head satisfies the standing UI review bar: no per-row projection scans, disclosure through real buttons, every reference resolved, and at least one handler mutation shown to be caught rather than survived. make ui is re-run and the regenerated internal/service/uidist embed is committed in the same head so make ui-check is clean. The exact head names its tests, publishes a successor artifact at ui retiring the live predecessor it covers, and requests review from an actor other than planner as its own durable request.","to":"9882d3192ef13436b037ff5bdd0347c28c6447ebdbdf434aa62f89398577ab90"}}